ir voice on  the video  but blamed their comments on the stress  of the job arising from the stress of  today's climate in law enforcement  cbs news reached out to the police union  and the three officers for comment  but never heard back it's one thing to  fire the officers  but you want more than that you want to  foreseeably prevent them from working in  law enforcement  again in the state of north carolina  correct that is correct  um normally when um officers are  involved in misconduct  they'll resign and they'll slip away  quietly and in some cases they'll  be able to maintain their certification  and get a job with another agency  in this case these individuals do not  deserve to be in law enforcement  chief williams even asked the district  attorney to review cases that the three  fired officers have been involved in to  look for biases  the d.a told cbs news 89 cases are under  review  and some have already been thrown out do  you think  you need more people who are black to be  on your force  i will say yes we also need more females  to be on that force  but the color of a person's skin  is not going to determine the color of  their heart you have  white officers that are good officers  you have white officers that are bad  officers you have black officers that  are good officers and you also have  black officers that are bad officers  so the color of their heart is more  important to me than the color of the  skin  boy how much do we love chief williams  that's such a good point me we all take  that message from him  but i got to tell you david listening to  those words was so hard to hear even  though they were  bleeped out that that is a police  officer on the force  who is who is supposedly to protect and  serve all of us  that's very tough to hear and painful  and painful thank  you thankfully it doesn't represent all  officers gail and would be great to have  a chief williams in every department  around the country  yes yes yes you could take notes 